    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's the formal 3-step progressive discipline process:\n\n1. Verbal Warning: Inform the employee of the specific performance issues and provide an opportunity for them to discuss and correct the problems.\n2. Written Warning: Issue a written document outlining the performance issues, the expected improvements, and the consequences of not meeting those expectations. This document should be dated, signed, and kept on file.\n3. Termination: If the employee fails to meet the expectations outlined in the written warning, terminate their employment. This should be done in accordance with your company's policies and procedures.\n\nKeep in mind that the specific steps and procedures may vary depending on your company's policies and local laws. It's always a good idea to consult with HR or your supervisor to ensure you're following the correct process.\n\nBy the way, I was just thinking, goblins are notorious for their love of paperwork and bureaucracy. They're always scribbling away in their cave journals, documenting every detail of their mischief.",
